FROM:
Eric Hammer, Planning and Development Department
DATE:
10/2/2017
SUBJECT:
Revised Maps for Interior Heights, 4th Filing Zone Change (UDC-17-00436)
and Replat (UDC-17-00437)
Dear City Councilmembers and Madam Mayor,
The City of Cheyenne Planning and Development Department has received a revised zone change map
for the Interior Heights 4th Filing Zoning Map Amendment, which is Item #9 on the Public Services
Committee agenda for tomorrow, October 3rd, 2017. In the staff report accompanying the application,
staff recommended the following conditions to the Governing Body:
1.
Correct the legal descrjtion of the subjectpropertyper comments by the Planning and
Development Department staffmembers.
2.
Change the zone change map to specify that one (1) unit is proposed, not four (4) units.
3.
Remove the 40’of York A venue ROW from the entitlement and map as it should not be a part of
this zoning map amendment.
This new map fulfills all three conditions that were recommended by staff and the Planning Commission.
Therefore, staff has changed our recommendation to anproval without conditions.
Additionally, the Planning and Development Department has received a revised final plat map for the
Interior Heights 4th Filing Final Plat application, which is Item #13 on the Public Services Committee
agenda for tomorrow, October
3Id, 2017. In the staff report accompanying the application, Staff
recommended the following conditions to the Governing Body:
1.
Correct the legal descrítion of the subject property per comments by Planning and Development
staffmembers.
2.
Correct the preilminary and final plat maps to show the required sets of City coordinates, as well
as required ties from City Control monuments, per comments by the City Surveyor.
3.
Remove all references to any re-dedication of the 40’ York A venue right-of-way from the
preliminary and final plats. References in the Municioal Acknowledgement, Plat Map, Entitlement,
and Dedication must be struck. The 40’ York A venue right-of-way may be shown on the plat map
with dashed lines, indicating it is outside of the boundaries of the proposed replat.
When
identifying the 40’ York A venue ri’ht-of-way, only reference the historic plat with which the ri’ht
of-way was established.
This new mao fulfills all three conditions that were recommended by staff and the Planning Commission.
Therefore, staff has chanced our recommendation to aroval without conditions.
```

